.TH WAVE-REINSTALL 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-reinstall \- Download and install the same version again, replacing what is on disk. Useful when a package was rebuilt under the same version number (4.6 relocated Mach-O files to @loader_path), when files were damaged, or to pin a package back to the version already installed instead of upgrading.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave reinstall <package>[@<version>] [, ...] | wave reinstall \-\-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download and install the same version again, replacing what is on disk.
Useful when a package was rebuilt under the same version number (4.6
relocated Mach-O files to @loader_path), when files were damaged, or to
pin a package back to the version already installed instead of
upgrading.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Reinstall every installed package
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-continue
Resume an interrupted download
.TP
.B \-\-proxy <string>
HTTP/HTTPS proxy (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080)
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-ssl
Skip SSL certificate verification (insecure)
.TP
.B \-\-limit\-rate <string>
Limit download speed (e.g. 200K, 1M, 5M; a bare number means bytes)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-time <string>
Maximum total time for one request (40s, 1min, 1min20s, 2h; a bare
number means seconds)
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-timeout <string>
Maximum time for the handshake
.TP
.B \-\-content\-time <string>
Maximum time to receive data
.TP
.B \-\-no\-link
Do not touch the unversioned link (the old name --unlink still works)
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-force
Install anyway when the running macOS is older than the package declares
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Plain output for logs and scripts: no emoji, no colours, ASCII progress
bar

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave reinstall jq
wave reinstall jq@1.8.2
wave reinstall jq, yq
wave reinstall --all
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
